<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Marcopolo launches Level One ADR.</title>
<headline>Brazil Marcopolo launches Level One ADR.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian largest bus body maker Marcopolo SA said it has launched a program of Level One American Depositary Receipts (ADRs).</p>
<p>The Marcopolo ADRs will be backed by existing shares and allow the company to be traded in the U.S. over-the-counter market, it said in a statement published in local newspapers.</p>
<p>Each ADR will represent 100 preferred shares, and Citibank will be coordinating the operation in the U.S., the statement said.</p>
<p>Brazilian private bank Itau will be the custodian bank in Brazil, it said.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
